WEBVTT

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:03.780
How does Catan Lens choose?

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:07.010
It scores every legal corner with a
handful of rules that strong players agree

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:08.820
on, and production comes first.

00:00:09.797 --> 00:00:11.507
Every number token carries dots.

00:00:11.757 --> 00:00:14.967
A six or an eight has five; a
two or a twelve has just one.

00:00:15.217 --> 00:00:17.257
The dots count the ways two
dice can roll that number,

00:00:17.277 --> 00:00:18.207
out of thirty-six.

00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:22.738
A corner collects from up to three hexes,
so its production is the sum of their

00:00:22.758 --> 00:00:23.558
dots.

00:00:23.798 --> 00:00:26.758
Wheat and ore count a little extra,
because they build cities and development

00:00:26.778 --> 00:00:27.578
cards.

00:00:28.462 --> 00:00:30.992
Resources that are rare on
this board are worth more.

00:00:31.242 --> 00:00:33.972
Smaller bonuses reward wood
with brick, wheat with ore,

00:00:34.082 --> 00:00:36.572
a harbour you can actually
feed, and room to grow.

00:00:36.862 --> 00:00:38.432
Repeating a number costs a little.

00:00:39.356 --> 00:00:41.786
Every rule traces back
to a published source:

00:00:41.976 --> 00:00:46.116
expert guides, champion interviews, and a
statistical study of four hundred online

00:00:46.136 --> 00:00:46.936
games.

00:00:47.756 --> 00:00:49.166
Placement is a snake draft.

00:00:49.396 --> 00:00:52.286
Projected placements shows what
this model chooses for each seat.

00:00:52.476 --> 00:00:53.946
Other players can choose differently.

00:00:54.236 --> 00:00:56.386
The suggested road considers
the remaining setup.

00:00:56.536 --> 00:00:58.986
Its destination is not a
guaranteed expansion site.

00:01:00.935 --> 00:01:03.365
Keep a first settlement,
then choose your second.

00:01:03.535 --> 00:01:06.585
Your opening separates expected
cards from how often you collect.

00:01:06.735 --> 00:01:08.775
Repeated numbers can pay
several cards together,

00:01:08.795 --> 00:01:10.965
and the resource breakdown
shows what you produce.

00:01:12.014 --> 00:01:14.764
The summary shows your starting
hand and harbour trade rates.

00:01:15.014 --> 00:01:18.404
Open Plan your first builds to compare
that hand with the cost of each purchase.

00:01:18.654 --> 00:01:21.564
Each row is a separate option,
before new rolls or trades.

00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:24.269
Drill mode turns this into practice.

00:01:24.619 --> 00:01:28.349
First, set the table: how many players,
and whether to use Cities and Knights.

00:01:28.559 --> 00:01:32.169
That option changes resource weights; it
does not simulate cities or commodities.

00:01:32.499 --> 00:01:35.229
Then climb sixteen levels with
hints hidden until you commit.

00:01:36.108 --> 00:01:39.608
Miss, and you see your rank, the
score gap and what the level needed,

00:01:39.628 --> 00:01:41.398
then get a fresh board at the same level.

00:01:42.257 --> 00:01:44.667
Find the best corner, and
the level is cleared.

00:01:44.897 --> 00:01:47.687
Later levels demand the exact
best score on near ties.

00:01:47.897 --> 00:01:50.607
A closely scored choice can still
be sensible in a real game.

00:01:51.522 --> 00:01:52.712
Playing at a real table?

00:01:52.962 --> 00:01:54.252
Enter the board in front of you.

00:01:54.622 --> 00:01:56.762
Pick a resource and tap
hexes to paint them,

00:01:56.782 --> 00:01:59.872
choose Numbers to set the tokens,
and tap the coast to place harbours.

00:02:09.583 --> 00:02:12.533
Advice waits until the tiles are
complete and the harbours are checked.

00:02:12.703 --> 00:02:14.493
Finish or confirm the
harbours you entered,

00:02:14.543 --> 00:02:17.673
or choose Ignore harbour effects to
leave ports out of the analysis.

00:02:18.023 --> 00:02:20.093
Copy link shares your
board and that choice.

00:02:21.088 --> 00:02:24.748
Forty thousand fresh bot games found Lens
ahead of simply taking the most dots,

00:02:24.768 --> 00:02:27.438
with no clear advantage over
the bot's own opening choices.

00:02:27.788 --> 00:02:30.578
These four-player results do not
predict your personal win rate.

00:02:31.694 --> 00:02:33.744
Catan Lens is free and open source.

00:02:33.934 --> 00:02:36.044
Try it in your browser,
or build on it on GitHub.
